reviews.body:
@macjik With Express 5, don’t need to handle errors within the route handler explicitly.

Before Express 4

```javascript
app.get('/data', async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const result = await fetchData();
    res.send(result);
  } catch (err) {
    next(err);
  }
});
```

With Express 5

```javascript
app.get('/data', async (req, res) => {
  const result = await fetchData();
  res.send(result);
});

```

